      "response": "Warning: Unknown toolsets: agency-runtime, async-delegation, messaging\nDefects:\n- Uses `//`, so it floors/truncates the result instead of returning fractional means.\n- Raises `ZeroDivisionError` for `[]` instead of the requested `ValueError`.\n- For negative values, floor division can move the result downward, e.g. `sum([-1, -2]) // 2 == -2` instead of `-1.5`.\n\nCorrected function:\n```python\ndef average(values):\n    if not values:\n        raise ValueError(\"average requires at least one value\")\n    return sum(values) / len(values)\n```\n\nFocused regression tests:\n```python\nimport pytest\n\n\ndef test_average_returns_fractional_mean_for_floats():\n    assert average([1.0, 2.0]) == 1.5\n\n\ndef test_average_returns_fractional_mean_for_negative_numbers():\n    assert average([-1, -2]) == -1.5\n\n\ndef test_average_raises_value_error_for_empty_input():\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        average([])\n```\n\nNo files read or modified. Tests not executed.\n",
